From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:13:46 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 177/207] Shard the graph proof host into serial test processes

Keep the compiler-discovered proof population and require complete execution receipts, including native failure controls. Retain the Zig SDK MIT license with the adapted runner.

Qualified 68 tests twice within 1984 MiB. Formatting, lean identity comparison and 22 project gates pass; plain build remains pending after a base-reproducible 2 GiB CUDA compiler OOM.

(cherry picked from commit 210f0d946c49fa1c03514b2aea02b6b8e213f860)
